# Abbreviations (map.txt, *abbreviations*) and the commands that define and remove them.

=== an abbreviation expands on <Space>
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"hh<Space>\" is expanded to \"hello<Space>\""
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh world<Esc>
expect: hello worl|d
mode:   normal

=== <C-]> expands without inserting a character
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"hh<C-]>\" is expanded to \"hello\""
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh<C-]>!<Esc>
expect: hello|!
mode:   normal

=== i_CTRL-] triggers an abbreviation
ref:    nvim/insert.txt *i_CTRL-]*
quote:  Trigger abbreviation, without inserting a character.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh<C-]><Esc>
expect: hell|o
mode:   normal

=== <Esc> ending Insert mode expands
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  This can also be the <Esc> that ends Insert mode
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh<Esc>
expect: hell|o
mode:   normal

=== a non-keyword character expands and is inserted after
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  The non-keyword character which ends the abbreviation is inserted after the expanded abbreviation.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh.<Esc>
expect: hello|.
mode:   normal

=== <CR> expands before the line break
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  An abbreviation is only recognized when you type a non-keyword character.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh<CR>x<Esc>
expect:
  hello
  |x
mode:   normal

=== a keyword character doesn't expand
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  An abbreviation is only recognized when you type a non-keyword character.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihhh -<Esc>
expect: hhh |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id: expanded after a space
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\" foo{CURSOR}\"   is expanded to \" four old otters\""
given:  |
keys:   :ab foo four old otters<CR>i foo<Esc>
expect:
   four old otter|s
mode:   normal

=== full-id: not expanded at the end of a longer word
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"barfoo{CURSOR}\"  is not expanded"
given:  |
keys:   :ab foo four old otters<CR>ibarfoo -<Esc>
expect: barfoo |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id: not expanded at the start of a longer word
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\" foobar{CURSOR}\" is not expanded"
given:  |
keys:   :ab foo four old otters<CR>i foobar -<Esc>
expect:
   foobar |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id: expanded where the insertion starts after a keyword
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  In front of the match is a non-keyword character, or this is where the line or insertion starts.
given:  ba|r
keys:   :iab foo X<CR>afoo -<Esc>
expect: barX |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id of one character isn't expanded after punctuation
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  When the abbreviation is only one character, it is not recognized if there is a non-keyword character in front of it, other than a space or a tab.
given:  |
keys:   :iab x why<CR>i.x -<Esc>
expect: .x |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id of one character is expanded after a space
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  When the abbreviation is only one character, it is not recognized if there is a non-keyword character in front of it, other than a space or a tab.
given:  |
keys:   :iab x why<CR>i( x -<Esc>
expect: ( why |-
mode:   normal

=== full-id of several characters is expanded after punctuation
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  In front of the match is a non-keyword character, or this is where the line or insertion starts.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>i(hh)<Esc>
expect: (hello|)
mode:   normal

=== end-id: expanded at the start of the line
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"#i{CURSOR}\"   is expanded to \"#include\""
given:  |
keys:   :ab #i #include<CR>i#i -<Esc>
expect: #include |-
mode:   normal

=== end-id: not expanded after a non-keyword character
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\">#i{CURSOR}\"   is not expanded"
given:  |
keys:   :ab #i #include<CR>i>#i -<Esc>
expect: >#i |-
mode:   normal

=== end-id: expanded after a keyword character
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  In front of the match is a keyword character, or a space or a tab, or this is where the line or insertion starts.
given:  |
keys:   :ab #i #include<CR>ia#i -<Esc>
expect: a#include |-
mode:   normal

=== non-id: not expanded after a keyword
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"test;;\"   is not expanded"
given:  |
keys:   :ab ;; <lt>endofline><CR>itest;;<Esc>
expect: test;|;
mode:   normal

=== non-id: expanded after a space
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  "\"test ;;\"   is expanded to \"test <endofline>\""
given:  |
keys:   :ab ;; <lt>endofline><CR>itest ;;<Esc>
expect: test <endofline|>
mode:   normal

=== non-id: expanded by <C-]>
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  An exception to this is the character <C-]>, which is used to expand an abbreviation without inserting any extra characters.
given:  |
keys:   :ab def# XX<CR>ix def#<C-]>-<Esc>
expect: x XX|-
mode:   normal

=== non-id: <Space> doesn't expand it
ref:    oracle nvim v0.11.7
given:  |
keys:   :ab def# XX<CR>ix def# -<Esc>
expect: x def# |-
mode:   normal

=== CTRL-V before the trigger avoids the expansion
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  To avoid the abbreviation in Insert mode: Type CTRL-V before the character that would trigger the abbreviation.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ihh<C-v><Space>x<Esc>
expect: hh |x
mode:   normal

=== typing the abbreviation in two inserts avoids it
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  Or type part of the abbreviation, exit insert mode with <Esc>, re-enter insert mode with "a" and type the rest.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>ih<Esc>ah -<Esc>
expect: hh |-
mode:   normal

=== abbreviations aren't recursive
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  You can use ":ab f f-o-o" without any problem.
given:  |
keys:   :ab f f-o-o<CR>if -<Esc>
expect: f-o-o |-
mode:   normal

=== an abbreviation works in Replace mode
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  Abbreviations are used in Insert mode, Replace mode and Command-line mode.
given:  |abcdefghij
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>Rhh <Esc>
expect: hello| ghij
mode:   normal

=== :ab abbreviations apply on the command line
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  Abbreviations are used in Insert mode, Replace mode and Command-line mode.
given:
  |a1
  a2
keys:   :ab ss s/a/b/<CR>:ss<CR>
expect:
  |b1
  a2
mode:   normal

=== :iab abbreviations don't apply on the command line
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:iabbrev*
quote:  same as ":ab", but for Insert mode only.
given:  |abc
keys:   :iab xx normal x<CR>:xx<CR>
expect: |abc
mode:   normal

=== :iab replaces an existing abbreviation
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:abbreviate-verbose*
quote:  If {lhs} already existed it is replaced with the new {rhs}.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>:iab hh howdy<CR>ihh<Esc>
expect: howd|y
mode:   normal

=== :iunabbrev removes an abbreviation
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:iunabbrev*
quote:  Same as ":una", but for insert mode only.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>:iuna hh<CR>ihh -<Esc>
expect: hh |-
mode:   normal

=== :unabbreviate by the rhs removes it
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:unabbreviate*
quote:  If none is found, remove abbreviations in which {lhs} matches with the {rhs}.
given:  |
keys:   :ab hh hello<CR>:una hello<CR>ihh -<Esc>
expect: hh |-
mode:   normal

=== :abclear removes all abbreviations
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:abclear*
quote:  Remove all abbreviations.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>:ab tt there<CR>:abclear<CR>ihh tt -<Esc>
expect: hh tt |-
mode:   normal

=== :iabclear removes the Insert mode abbreviations
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:iabclear*
quote:  Remove all abbreviations for Insert mode.
given:  |
keys:   :iab hh hello<CR>:iabclear<CR>ihh -<Esc>
expect: hh |-
mode:   normal

=== an abbreviation can be mapped through
ref:    nvim/map.txt *abbreviations*
quote:  But abbreviations can be mapped.
given:  |
keys:   :imap Q hello<CR>:iab hh Q<CR>ihh -<Esc>
expect: hello |-
mode:   normal

=== :inoreabbrev isn't mapped
ref:    nvim/map.txt *:inoreabbrev*
quote:  same as ":ab", but for Insert mode only and no remapping for this {rhs}
given:  |
keys:   :imap Q hello<CR>:inorea hh Q<CR>ihh -<Esc>
expect: Q |-
mode:   normal
